# Normalise line endings across this repository.
#
# Why this file exists: on 2026-08-27 every code repo in the project reported its
# entire tree as rewritten -- thousands of insertions and deletions with zero
# content change, purely CRLF vs LF. The index stored LF while the Windows
# working tree stored CRLF. That stayed invisible locally only because Git for
# Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config; any checkout without it
# (CI, a Linux clone, a cold index) saw the whole tree as modified. `git diff`
# was useless for review and real edits were buried in the noise -- one genuine
# 43-line change in `cloud` was invisible until whitespace was filtered out.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores AND checks out every text file with LF, so the index
# and the working tree agree regardless of any machine's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# One-time cleanup after adding this file:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings to LF (.gitattributes)"
# Do that as its own commit, on a clean tree, so the noise is isolated to it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shells need real CRLF on disk.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.webp    binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.docx    binary
*.pptx    binary
*.zip     binary
*.jar     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.mp4     binary
*.mwb     binary
*.mwb.bak binary
